# Admin Pages Development Guide

## 1. Admin Login + Auth
Create an admin login page at /admin route.
- Email and password fields
- Hardcoded credentials: admin@example.com / admin123
- On success → redirect to /admin/dashboard
- On failure → show "Invalid credentials" error
- Store login state using React Context or localStorage
- Protect all /admin/* routes (redirect to login if not authenticated)

Use the same styling as existing components in this project.
## 2. Admin Dashboard
Create an admin dashboard layout with sidebar at /admin/dashboard.

Sidebar navigation links:
- Dashboard (icon: home)
- Users (icon: users) → /admin/users
- Problem Requests (icon: inbox) → /admin/problem-requests
- Contests (icon: trophy) → /admin/contests
- Admin Profile (icon: user) → /admin/profile

Main content area shows 4 statistic cards:
- Total Users (show number from API/dummy data)
- Total Problems (show number)
- Active Today (show number)
- Total Problems Pending (show number)

Use Tailwind CSS. Make it responsive. The sidebar should be collapsible on mobile.

## 3. User Management Page
Create a user management page at /admin/users.

Features:
1. User Table with columns: Username, Solved Problems Count, Level
2. Each row has an "Actions" button that opens a dropdown/modal with:
   - Ban User (shows a form for feedback reason)
   - Unban User
   - Remove Account

Behavior:
- After clicking "Ban User" → show form asking "Reason for ban" → submit → show toast "Banned successfully"
- After "Unban User" → show toast "Unbanned successfully"
- After "Remove Account" → show confirmation modal "Are you sure?" → on confirm → show "Account removed successfully"

Use dummy data for now (create an array of 5-10 sample users with different statuses).
Style matches the existing dashboard.

## 4. Problem Request Page
Create a problem request page at /admin/problem-requests.

Features:
1. Table showing requested problems with columns:
   - Title
   - Difficulty (Easy/Medium/Hard)
   - Status (Pending/Approved/Rejected)
   - Action (View Problem button)

2. Click "View Problem" → opens a modal showing:
   - Problem title, description, examples, constraints
   - Same interface as user problem page, but WITHOUT code editor/IDE
   - Two buttons: "Approve" and "Reject"

3. Approve button → changes status to Approved → show toast "Problem approved"

4. Reject button → shows a form for feedback message (textarea) → submit → show toast "Feedback sent successfully" → status becomes Rejected

Use dummy data with 5-10 sample problem requests.

## 5. Contest Management Page
Create a contest management page at /admin/contests with two sections:

SECTION 1 - Contest List (top):
- Table showing all contests with columns:
  | Contest Name | Start Time | Duration | Status (Upcoming/Ongoing/Ended) |
- Each row has Edit, Delete, and End Contest buttons

SECTION 2 - Create Contest Form (bottom/side):
Fields:
- Contest Name (text input)
- Description (textarea)
- Start Time (datetime-local)
- End Time (datetime-local)
- Problem Selection (button that opens Problem Dashboard)

PROBLEM SELECTION MODAL:
- Shows all available problems with checkboxes
- Admin can tick ✓ to add problem or ✗ to remove
- Selected problems list shows below

Additional buttons for each contest:
- Edit Contest (opens prefilled form)
- Delete Contest (confirmation modal)
- End Contest manually (only for ongoing contests)

Use dummy data for contests and problems.

## 6. Admin Profile Page
Create an admin profile page at /admin/profile showing:
- Profile picture (placeholder)
- Name: Admin
- Email: admin@example.com
- Role: Super Admin
- Join date: [current date]

Options:
- Change Password (modal with current password, new password, confirm)
- Logout button (clears auth, redirects to /admin/login)

Style matches the dashboard.